==========================================================================
CORRECTION appended after the run, by the author of the script.
==========================================================================
The "SPEEDUP" line above is WRONG as a replacement cost and must not be
quoted.  This file measured slices + C_b extraction + factorisations, and
SKIPPED PART 1 -- the cross-component H-orthogonality of anchor_wtest.py.
PART 1 is REQUIRED, not optional: without it W^T H W may carry off-diagonal
blocks, so positive definiteness of the diagonal blocks proves nothing about
the Gram; it is also what supplies joint independence, since "sum dim = B"
here is a sum of per-component dimensions computed with separate pivot
tables.  The file's own header said the comparison must be end to end; the
code was not.

Honest replacement cost, PART 1 timings from anchor_wtest_n{5,6}.log:
    B= 350:  107 s + 29 s  =  136 s  vs control  193 s  =>  1.4x
    B= 702:  897 s + 283 s = 1180 s  vs control 2201 s  =>  1.9x
    B=1274:  PART 1 not run at n=7; the 1913 s above is the C_b build ALONE
             and is NOT a replacement cost.  (7,4)'s check [4] is NOT closed
             by this run.

What survives unchanged: the VERDICTS agree with the control, and the exact
factorisations are near-free -- 1 s at n=6 against a 2201 s control.  The
cost moved into the slice build and the orthogonality check, both O(B^3).

anchor_cb_measure.py has since been corrected to print the honest figure and
to refuse a speedup at any n where PART 1's cost is not recorded.
==========================================================================
